  "description": "ODURAH crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H141 N18 Na1 Nd12 O92,39(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1J (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1B (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1I (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1K (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2J (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2B (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2I (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2K (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.072-4.220 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 110.08-115.94°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C102H219Nd12N18NaO131. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 12 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 39 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
